# MiniShop — Kubernetes Learning Platform (On-Prem, Windows)
### A mini production-style system covering all core K8s concepts

---

## 0. Goals & Constraints

- **Goal:** learn K8s from primitives → production patterns by building one coherent 3-tier web app ("MiniShop") on a real multi-node cluster.
- **Host:** Windows 11, Intel Core 14th-gen, 32GB RAM, 256GB disk.
- **Constraints:** free/OSS only, popular/well-documented tools, automated provisioning, fast iteration, lightweight footprint (target ≤10GB RAM peak).
- **App strategy:** reuse an existing open-source demo app (`kumahq/kuma-demo`'s marketplace app) rather than building frontend/backend from scratch — saves implementation tokens/time, keeps focus on K8s mechanics rather than app code.
- **Output of this phase:** design doc + implementation plan only. Actual manifest/script authoring is a separate step done by an implementation assistant.

---

## 1. Tech Stack & Rationale

| Concern | Choice | Why this over alternatives |
|---|---|---|
| Container runtime | **Docker Desktop (WSL2 backend)** | Best-supported on Windows; free for personal/learning use. |
| Cluster provisioner | **kind** (Kubernetes IN Docker) | Runs *real* upstream K8s — etcd, kube-apiserver, kube-scheduler, kube-controller-manager appear as actual static pods. Multi-node cluster up in ~60-90s. |
| **Application source** | **`kumahq/kuma-demo` marketplace app** (Vue frontend + Node/Express backend), pre-built Docker Hub images, **patched, not rebuilt from source** | Closest existing OSS app matching your stack: frontend + backend + Postgres + Redis, in one repo, with working images. See Section 6a for exactly what's kept/stripped/added. |
| Package manager | **Helm 3** | Industry standard; installs all infra add-ons in one command each. |
| Env templating (own app) | **Kustomize** | Ships inside `kubectl` (`kubectl apply -k`), zero install. |
| Ingress controller | **ingress-nginx** | Most widely deployed, official Kind-specific install path. |
| LoadBalancer impl. | **MetalLB** | Standard way *on-prem* clusters get real `type: LoadBalancer` IPs. |
| Dynamic storage | **local-path-provisioner** (Rancher) | <50MB, zero-config dynamic PVs. |
| Database + Operator/CRD | **CloudNativePG (CNPG)** | Popular CNCF-sandbox Postgres operator; one `Cluster` CRD gives primary+replica, failover, backups. Replaces kuma-demo's un-persisted single Postgres Deployment. |
| Cache (manual StatefulSet) | **Redis**, raw manifests, PVC added | Deliberately kept as a raw StatefulSet (not operator-managed) to contrast with CNPG's abstraction. |
| Metrics for autoscaling | **metrics-server** | Required by HPA. |
| Monitoring | **kube-prometheus-stack** | De facto production combo, one Helm install. |

